OUTPUT FORMAT
Use <think> once for your reasoning about which terms matter most, then output the keywords grouped into up to 4 priority tiers. Skip a tier entirely if it has nothing in it.

<think>
brief reasoning here
</think>
<items_1>
keyword text | category
keyword text | category
</items_1>
<items_2>
keyword text | category
</items_2>
<items_3>
keyword text | category
</items_3>
<items_4>
keyword text | category
</items_4>

Tier meaning:
- items_1: required, explicitly stated, and emphasized or mentioned more than once
- items_2: required, explicitly stated, mentioned once
- items_3: clearly implied as necessary for the role but not phrased as a formal requirement
- items_4: preferred / nice-to-have

Each line inside an items block is exactly: the keyword text, then " | ", then one category from skill|tool|title|certification|methodology|domain|experience. One keyword per line. Nothing else.